From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dbgeng: live debugging, symbols, expressions and commands (3590)

dbgeng: live debugging, symbols, expressions and commands

Builds the debugger engine on top of 3008 (data spaces, system objects and
the state queries).

Targets: CreateProcess, CreateProcess2, CreateProcessAndAttach(2) and
invasive AttachProcess run the debuggee through the debugging interface;
WaitForEvent delivers create/exit process and thread, module load/unload,
exception, breakpoint, debug string and system error events to the event
callbacks (plain, wide or context flavour) and applies the event and
exception filters, the engine options (initial break, initial module break,
final break) and the callbacks' answers. SetExecutionStatus drives go,
handled/not handled and single step; software breakpoints (IDebugBreakpoint
and IDebugBreakpoint2 objects, flags, pass counts, thread match, offset
expressions, commands) are inserted while the target runs and stepped over.
WriteDumpFile(2) writes a minidump.

Symbols and types go through dbghelp: GetNameByOffset, GetOffsetByName,
GetNearNameByOffset, line lookups, symbol matches, module lookups, type id,
name, size, field offset and name, enumerator names, typed data
read/write/output, scope, symbol groups (scope and created, with expansion),
symbol and source entries, source file search, synthetic modules and symbols,
function entries.

Control: Evaluate/CoerceValue (MASM and C++ style expressions, registers,
symbols, memory dereference operators), Execute and ExecuteCommandFile with
aliases and a command set (?, r, k*, d*, e*, u, x, ln, dt, lm, bp/bl/bc/bd/be,
sx*, g/p/t, as/ad/al, .echo, .sympath, .logopen ...), stack traces,
disassembly through the bundled capstone, log files, text macros and
replacements, event filters, prompts, extensions, output line prefixes,
system version and time queries. The wide variants forward to the narrow ones.

include/dbgeng.h gets the constants, IID_IDebugSymbolGroup and the right
parameter types and names of a few methods (GetCurrentTimeDate,
GetCurrentSystemUpTime, GetManagedStatus, GetTextReplacement ...).

